t?  Because a big part of what makes a winning AI ad   or actually a winning ad in general is how good  the hook is, right? A hundred percent. I would   say everyone focuses on the written hook. So this  is probably 50% of the results. And also a super   important thing is the visual hook. what do we see  in the first second? And we will talk about that   in the future of this video because you can also,  with AI, create some crazy stuff to hook people's   attention very early on. They decide to scroll  on an ad in a millisecond, right? So you need   to hook them even visually before they listen  to the beginning of the script. But with this,   you can generate the first sentence. And I  think it generates very good hooks because   it was trained on so many hooks that we had in our  database. why did most people give up on learning   a new language? I think it's a very, very good  hook. So you can save multiple ones, save the ones   you really , delete the ones you don't , and just  start making a collection of hooks right here.   And then you can just copy paste them all and put  them into a Google Sheets. Then once you have your   hook, and I actually use the hook generator to get  this one that I really . True fact, most people   never stick with learning a new language. Once  I got that, I just wrote the rest of the script   using Cloud as well. And I got the script right  here that you can then use with an AI actor. So we   have this library of now over a thousand AI actors  that you can use, where you can use filters to   just find the perfect AI actor for your needs. So  you can filter on the gender, obviously the age,   and some cool situations this. You know, when you  are doing these UGC content, So for the audience,   you see user-generated content. It's content where  there is someone talking to the camera. When you   do this type of content, you will always want  to have a specific type of creators promote your   video, and they will be doing something specific.  So I don't know if you have an idea for a podcast   ad where you want people to be in a studio, a  nice setup where they talk about your product   in a nice configuration, you can just select the  podcast filter. If you have, for example, I saw on   your website the ID browser that you have, this  idea for pregnant women and this trend that was   growing. Maybe you have a product that targets  pregnant women and you want to have someone who   is pregnant in your video. Or maybe you want to  have a funny skit-style interview where someone   is talking from the side, if they are talking to  a friend. We got all sorts of filters that you   can use. If you have a fitness product, maybe you  might want to have people in the gym. You can play   with these filters or even with accessories that  they have. If you want them to have, let's say,   a laptop, for example, you can use that filter  and you will only see AI avatars talking next to   a laptop. You can select the emotions and even  the skin tone of the AI actor. And the beauty   of AI is now instead of just selecting one person  to talk in your video, you can just generate five   variations. And our most successful customers, and  that's really the first tip I really want to share   with your audience, our most successful customers,  they really go crazy about testing. They test   the hoops or every single script that they do  because now with AI, in a couple of minutes,   they can generate so many variations. They will  test different actors, different hoops, different   situations. And really the results can be  completely different when they do that properly.   So yeah, you will select an actor. You can see the  preview of the actor before you generate. And then   you can tweak the audio. We'll see all the details  of how we can optimize the results in a minute.   But you can tweak the audio. Click Generate, wait  a couple of seconds, and I already have this video   that was generated with the script for Duolingo,  and you get a result this. Here you go. Now   you get your video, and we'll talk about that as  well if you want, Greg, but you can then edit it,   remove the background, show your app, and most of  all, test a lot of different versions of the exact   same app. Sam Altman, the co-founder of OpenAI,  I just said that it is the era of the idea guy   and he is not wrong. I think that right now is an  incredible time to be building a startup. And if   you listen to this podcast, chances are you think  so, too. Now, I think that you can look at trends   to basically figure out what are the startup  ideas you should be building. So that's exactly   why I built idea browser dot com. Every single  day, you're going to get a free startup idea in   your inbox, and it's all backed by high-quality  data trends. How we do it, people always ask. We   use AI agents to go and search, what are people  looking for, and what are they screaming for in   terms of products that you should be building?  And then we hand it on a silver platter for you   to go check out. We do have a few paid plans  that, you know, take it to the next level,   give you more ideas, give you more AI agents and  more almost a chat GBT for ideas with it. But   you can start for free, ideabrowser.com. And if  you're listening to this, I highly recommend it.   So I'm seeing a trend right now with two types  of AI ads. And I think about it, you know,   from a spectrum. On one side of the spectrum,  you have extremely realistic ads. ad. And on the   other side of the spectrum, you have unrealistic  scroll stopping ads. And what I mean by that,   that is this morning I saw a gorilla, a talking  gorilla VO3 ad, I think. And there's also the Star   Wars. I don't know if you saw the Star Wars selfie  ads. So what you're saying, Roman, is basically   sometimes it makes sense to, Well, it makes sense  that the more the better because you're kind of   doing R\u0026D to find the winning ad that can get you  your CAC to LTV ratio in the place. But would you   agree that it's helpful to have, if you're selling  a pregnancy product, having maybe pregnancy women   as an actor, but also maybe some unrealistic,  funny, other types of scroll stomping videos   and then sort of testing them to see what works?  100%. So before creating our cards, I was actually   growing a mobile app studio and all I was doing  was testing a ton of ads every day. It was before   the age of AI but really the two criteria for us  to succeed was the creative volume so how many   new creatives did we produce every single week  that was the number one criteria and the second   one was the creative diversity and the diversity  is which type of creative do you test because if   you only test talking actors, for example,  these ones, or if you only test gorilla video,   at some point, your audience will kind of fatigue  and there is this concept called creative fatigue   in the world of paid advertising and people  will just stop engaging. So yeah, creative   diversity is super important and that's actually  our vision at Arcade. We think AI is completely   going to transform the way marketing teams create  content and we think that There is going to be   one platform where marketers create all sorts of  content and optimize for the results. So we have,   for example, you mentioned the Gorilla example.  We have a VO3 integration where you can actually   generate those Gorilla videos and you can actually  do more. I'm going to show you that in a second.   So to your point, you need to be testing both.  you need to be testing real UGC-style videos, more   creative stuff, and even other types of videos  that I can show you in the demo if you want. And   that being said, there are certain niches where we  see very good results for some reason with AI UGC,   and for some reason, it's just performing better  in these niches. I can show you some examples,   if you want, of successful customers who  are using archives and getting really,   really good results. And then I can show you how  you can use the archives to also regenerate those   less realistic videos, the Lego ones that we  see here that I'm going to show you in a minute   as well. Okay. Yeah one example of that is one  of our clients Codeway So it a mobile app studio   They own multiple apps and they launched this  app as you can see here on September 2024 so   actually less than 12 months ago And last month,  they made a million in revenue. And that's just,   by the way, the iOS app. They also have an Android  app. So they made in total more than 15 million in   revenue with this app, and that's all public data,  by the way. And when you look at their ads in the   Facebook ads library, is the Facebook ad library,  is this public library where you can see the ads   of any advertiser, you will see two things. One,  they test a ton of new ads every week. So if you   look at the total results, they have 500 active  ads because we filtered on active. Just yesterday,   they started a new ad. So if you just filter on ,  literally yesterday we are recording on July 22,   they were testing maybe five, 10 ads that we can  see right here for this single app and they have   multiple apps. And the thing that is interesting  about this page is they are testing a ton of ads,   but all of them are AI. This app was launched  literally nine months ago, and every single ad   that they tested was AI-generated using ArcAds,  and that's the whole marketing strategy that they   had for this app. They basically created ads using  ArcAds, and I can show you one of the ads that was   bringing the most results, and it's a very  realistic ad, but to your point, They test   some realistic concept, but they also test  these robot-style video ads where there   is someone talking. And by the way, as you can  see, they localize everything in every language,   which is also one of the nice things about AI.  You can now, instead of just targeting one geo,   if you want to have, I don't know even what  language this is, but if you want to have those   20, 50 languages in your ads on German, English,  Russian, et cetera, it will be a nightmare to find   creators in every single country. Now with AI,  you can just do that in every single country super   easily. So I use this tool called PPAds to track  impressions of ads. Again, that's public data. And   as you can see, this ad right here had 10 million  impressions. That was the most viral ad that they   had. And they combined the two worlds. They  had this realistic AI UGC at the bottom created   with ArcAd, and they combined that with a less  realistic video. And they basically made a video   about this person trying to learn a new language.  So yeah, again, if you wanted to have someone with   a Spanish accent talking and learning English, it  would be super time-concerning to produce that.   They literally produce that in a couple of seconds  and using AI. And by the way, I can show you very   quickly how you can do this kind of stuff, but  I'll pause here in case you have any question.   Now, dude, this is, keep going. This is the sauce  that I need. Perfect. So, yeah. So when you have   a script, I just click on Remix right here.  What this does is it will put the script in   the model right here to let me just reuse the same  script. And maybe I will get very good results   with this ad. So I want to try new variations  of this ad. I want to change maybe the hook. I   want to add additional actors. Or I want to change  the accents. and you can do that now with Archads   right here because you can go to the voiceover and  you can do two things. You can either use one of   our existing voices in our library. So let's say  you want to have a Spanish accent right here. You   will be able to say Spanish. You will have all of  these Spanish voices that we had and you can even   control the accent of these voices. Maybe you want  to do someone with a Spanish