something I would recommend   people doing. You can also just go to another AI  tool and generate an image of someone you think   looks really well, looks really good. and create  your own custom avatar from an image that you   upload from MidJourney. So for example, this one  that you see right here, the one in the podcast,   I generated it from MidJourney. So I generated an  image of someone looking that in MidJourney. And   then I brought that into archives and I generated  an AI actor from this image. And by the way,   again, this was inspired from Bifred. I saw  these ads. They were running for quite a   long time. So I assumed it was doing well. and  basically I recreated, I screenshot did this,   I sent that to Claude or ChatGPT and I asked  them, describe what you see in the video. That   gave me a prompt. I used it as a prompt to make  journey and then I uploaded the image into Arcade   to create my own AI actor instead of using one  of the actors in the library that was available.   And obviously this actor is only available on my  account. You can do super creative concepts using   that and that's a very efficient way to use the  platform. But coming back to your point for VO3,   you probably saw this trend on Twitter where  you can do unboxing videos using VO3. And yeah,   I basically just use this prompt with our scenes  feature. Let's use this VO3 in the background   and recreated this unboxing video. And then I  thought, OK, what if I could do this for Lego   instead of Ikea? because, you know, IKEA, it's  an interesting concept for IKEA because at IKEA,   you create stuff. And Lego is also somewhere  where you create stuff. So I made this video   right here using the same prompt, basically, but  for Lego. And then here you go. You get a video of   a bunch of Legos being built. But then I thought,  okay, it would be nicer if it was in a nicer room,   a kid's room, actually. So I just clicked Remix  right here. It added the prompt automatically   to the bar here. and I changed a little bit the  description to have the video be in a kid's room.   And here you go. The limitation of VO3 is, you  know, you get those eight second videos, which   are nice, but when you want to do a marketing  campaign, you want a little bit more than that.   You might want to have something happening after  the end of this video. And we recently released   this feature called Extend. So basically what it  does is it lets you select a frame in the video.   So the frame where you want the next video to  start and uses that as the starting point for   a new video that's going to be generated. And  that's kind of insane because now once you have   these videos that you liked, you can just keep the  exact same consistency and generate the rest of   the video. What happens after that in the video?  And you can have a kid that was actually hidden   right here, join the scene and start playing  with the Lego. And then you can do it again,   click extend again. and maybe you want his little  sister to join the video. And then you can, again,   extend the video and the little sister is  joining the frame with perfect consistency.   So that's the same boy right here. And now  you have those three eight-second videos that   you can combine together and make a full video  production with perfect consistency. Insanity.   Yeah, that's really, really good. do you want me  to talk about automation? I do because it's a bit   of a black box for me. I've been playing with it,  but I'm just, I just, yeah, I want to hear from,   you know, from you just the best practices around  automation. Yeah, a hundred percent. So I think   you, you, you got the founder of Gumloop on the  podcast a couple of weeks ago. I really their   team and their tool. And I think he actually, in  this video, he explained very well what is a good   case for an automation. And an automation is when  you can clearly explain every single step of your   process, but it will be very time-consuming to  repeat them. So the way I think about automation   for arcads is I think about all the repetitive  stuff that I do when it comes to producing ads   and I see if I can automate these And one of the  most repetitive tasks of any marketer is to look   for inspiration, look at what the competitors  are doing, use that as inspiration to create new   content. So I created this automation in GameLoop,  I can show my screen and show you, where you can   basically input a keyword. So for us, for example,  I wanted to promote arcades, so create content   about AI UGC and about arcades on TikTok. So I  created this node right here that I connected to   a TikTok downloader that will basically take all  the videos that were posted on TikTok about these   keywords through the TikTok API, Downloading the  videos, transcribe them. So if there is someone   talking in the video, it gets what's being said in  the videos. And then brings that automatically to   ChatVPT with a quick description of my product.  So my product is, which is linked to this note   right here where I describe Arcade's AI ad maker.  So my product is Arcade's AI ad maker. Here is a   very good transcript of a TikTok video. So this is  the TikTok video that it's scraped from the TikTok   API. Write a similar script about my product. Make  sure to stick to the writing style to keep it very   similar to the transcript I provided, but make it  about my product. And then, and that's the beauty   of AI automation, I connected it to an Arcade  node. So if you search for AI video in Gumblup,   you will see that you have Arcade as one of the  nodes that you can connect. And it will basically   generate the script that is inspired from all  the videos that have been posted on TikTok and   that's ranked well on TikTok because the API will  automatically search for the highest view videos.   And it will generate videos that will be inspired  from winning videos automatically for me. That's   one very good example. I have a ton of use cases  and I can show you more. So that's one very good   example of how you can use Arcade's API to connect  with external sources of data to automatically   produce winning ads. And that's the advanced mode  of AI video generation, but that's very powerful.   Dude, can you show me more? Yeah, 100%. So I  really this one for TikTok because I think on   TikTok you'll find very good content. But I also  made an equivalent for Reddit. And I know you   are a fan of Reddit. I know you love Reddit.  so basically this one is a bit more complex,   the automation is a bit more complex so people  can reach out if they want to talk about how   to set this up on their own basically I created  this AI agent with GameLoop again sorry can you   make a full screen? yes right here you go, so it  will find the most popular posts on Reddit and   it will add them to a Google sheet, it will go  to Orcad, this was the previous user interface,   to generate different videos. And basically what  it takes is it collects the most, goes to the most   popular subreddit in your niche. It collects  the top questions, it feeds them to chat GPT,   it generates scripts from that, and it generates  videos using Orcad. So basically all you need is   an inspiration. For the previous example, the  inspiration was TikTok and AI to take this   inspiration and rewrite it in a way that will be  a good ad and then an API to generate the video,   which is ArcAds. It's pretty much always this.  Another example of that is scraping the ads   library. So in GameLoop they have a node where  the source of the data can be the Facebook ad   library. So you can actually download videos from  your competitors from their Facebook ad library,   send that to a Google sheet and then rewrite those  ads using AI. And that's also a very powerful way   to automate ad creation. You will find a lot  of them on my Twitter account if you want to   see more examples of that. Maybe one last one. So  all of these I just showed you were about taking   the transcript of an existing video and rewriting  the script to create a new video inspired from the   script. So basically what this will do is really,  it will complete the script of the talking actor.   So if we go back to Arcades, it will complete this  part of the text box right here. But sometimes you   want to recreate a video and what you need is  not really a script, you need a prompt. Let's   say you want to generate a video this, you  want this description of what's happening,   you don't want the voiceover of the video, right?  and if you want to do that, what you will need   to analyze is not the transcript of an existing  video, you will need to analyze the visual of an   existing video. And Gemini, you know, the Google  AI API lets you basically analyze existing videos   and tells you what's happening in the video.  Does that make sense? Yeah, absolutely. So you   can basically go to the ad library of a competitor  this, send the video to Gemini, and ask Gemini,   describe what you see in the video. Describe  what happens in these videos scene by scene.   And this will give you the prompt to generate  with our VO3 integration AI videos. and yeah,   let's say you need to have basketball players, you  will need a prompt to say, I want to generate a   basketball player and Gemino can give you this  prompt and then you can send that back to our   Sins mobile and complete automatically this part  of the script. What a crazy world we live in. It   is, yeah, so many every day I talk to an archives  customer who is making seven, eight figures using   these AI ads. And again, I learned about a new  super creative stuff. And sometimes the niche I   hear about, you will be surprised how niche and  how small they seem and how much money people   are making. I mean, I can give you other examples,  but yeah, it's crazy how people are getting insane   results with these ads. Yeah, and I think it's  worth noting that not